card.statement:
Let $A=\TGWA{R}{\si}{t}{\mu}$ be any twisted generalized Weyl algebra.
Let $V$ be any simple weight module over $A$ such that $\Stab(\mf)=\{0\}$
for $\mf\in\Supp(V)$. Then $V\simeq A/N(\mf)$ where $A$ is considered as
a left module over itself and $N(\mf)$ is the left ideal given by

\begin{equation}
N(\mf)=\{a\in A\mid F(b,a)\in\mf \;\forall b\in A\}
\end{equation}
